WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:02.540
Manager!

00:02.540 --> 00:04.970
Can you please bring that thing we've been talking about?

00:04.970 --> 00:05.980
Yes.

00:05.980 --> 00:11.910
It's a familiar taste. It's the stamina drink my wife made with milk and honey that she's so proud of.

00:11.910 --> 00:14.410
Make sure you drink up! Take it to the match!

00:14.410 --> 00:15.370
Yes!

00:15.370 --> 00:19.460
This really gets us going before a match. We couldn't do it without this drink, coach!

00:20.040 --> 00:21.120
You really think so?

00:21.120 --> 00:22.920
Here you go, Matsuyama.

00:22.920 --> 00:24.080
Okay, thank you!

00:26.710 --> 00:33.050
By the way, this is the last tournament where you'll be taking care of us. Right, Fujisawa?

00:34.160 --> 00:35.050
Yeah...

00:37.560 --> 00:40.310
<i>Man, it's cold.</i>

00:40.310 --> 00:44.730
<i>When it snows while you're dressed in thick clothes, you end up sweating and feeling even colder.</i>

00:44.730 --> 00:47.560
<i>Here, Matsuyama, Oda. Take these.</i>

00:48.230 --> 00:50.260
<i>Wipe your sweat with this.</i>

00:50.260 --> 00:51.530
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:53.280 --> 00:54.610
<i>It's warm!</i>

00:54.610 --> 00:57.620
<i>Yoshiko warmed them up for you in front of the stove.</i>

00:57.620 --> 01:00.330
<i>You did? You're so thoughtful.</i>

01:05.060 --> 01:12.220
<i>Yoshiko Fujisawa will be moving to the US in the second term, due to her father's work.</i>

01:16.850 --> 01:22.550
As your final memory before you transfer, I'll show you how we become the national champions.

01:22.550 --> 01:23.600
Yeah.

01:26.140 --> 01:27.700
Come on, give me some!

01:27.700 --> 01:29.110
Oh, sorry.

01:29.110 --> 01:33.900
Don't run out of stamina during the game because of this heat.

01:33.900 --> 01:37.410
After all, we're not used to such sultry weather.

01:37.410 --> 01:39.460
It'll be all right, coach.

01:39.460 --> 01:43.410
No one has gotten worn out so far, and everybody's been improving their track record.

01:43.410 --> 01:44.690
You're right.

01:44.690 --> 01:49.520
Moreover, we also have this stamina drink your beautiful wife made for us.

01:49.520 --> 01:50.670
You little bastard...

01:52.300 --> 01:56.970
But guys, the more we win and advance, the stronger our opponents get.

01:56.970 --> 01:58.260
Don't let your guard down.

01:58.760 --> 02:03.310
Today's opponent, Minamiuwa, is a good team with a well-balanced offense and defense.

02:03.310 --> 02:09.940
Pay particular attention to their captain Ishida's technique, and their center forward Takei's powerful headers.

02:04.060 --> 02:09.060
FW, TAKEI

02:04.060 --> 02:09.060
CAPTAIN, ISHIDA

02:09.940 --> 02:11.360
Yes!

02:11.360 --> 02:14.580
All right! If we win, we'll practically be set up to play against Nankatsu.

02:14.580 --> 02:17.770
To get there, we must completely break Minamiuwa down!

02:17.770 --> 02:18.700
Yeah!

02:19.570 --> 02:20.980
<i>Yoshiko...</i>

02:20.980 --> 02:23.830
<i>Can't you open up to Matsuyama and say that you love him?</i>

02:23.830 --> 02:27.140
<i>If you can't do it today, then...</i>

02:31.250 --> 02:33.960
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:31.250 --> 02:33.960
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:34.880 --> 02:37.550
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:34.880 --> 02:37.550
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:38.460 --> 02:41.180
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:38.460 --> 02:41.180
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:48.060 --> 02:50.890
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

02:48.060 --> 02:50.890
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

02:50.890 --> 02:57.150
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

02:50.890 --> 02:57.150
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

02:57.150 --> 03:03.030
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta no ni</i>

02:57.150 --> 03:03.030
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

03:03.030 --> 03:09.620
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

03:03.030 --> 03:09.620
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

03:09.620 --> 03:13.620
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

03:09.620 --> 03:13.620
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

03:13.620 --> 03:18.130
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

03:13.620 --> 03:18.130
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

03:18.130 --> 03:23.680
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

03:18.130 --> 03:23.680
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

03:23.680 --> 03:25.260
<i>baka darou?</i>

03:23.680 --> 03:25.260
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

03:25.260 --> 03:26.470
<i>ai</i>

03:25.260 --> 03:26.470
<i>Love!</i>

03:26.470 --> 03:29.970
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

03:26.470 --> 03:29.970
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

03:29.970 --> 03:39.860
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

03:29.970 --> 03:39.860
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

03:39.860 --> 03:40.690
<i>ai</i>

03:39.860 --> 03:40.690
<i>Love!</i>

03:40.690 --> 03:44.490
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

03:40.690 --> 03:44.490
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

03:44.490 --> 03:48.490
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

03:44.490 --> 03:48.490
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

03:48.490 --> 03:54.750
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

03:48.490 --> 03:54.750
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

03:54.750 --> 03:57.540
<i>hanasanai</i>

03:54.750 --> 03:57.540
<i>for a single moment!</i>

03:59.760 --> 04:05.510
<b><b>EPISODE 40:
FURANO GOES TO WAR</b></b>

04:00.960 --> 04:04.740
<i>It's the second game of the quarter finals of the National Middle School Football Tournament.</i>

04:04.740 --> 04:08.510
<i>The match between Toho Academy and Chubu MS is about to end.</i>

04:08.510 --> 04:13.850
<i>Toho makes their first-year player, Sawada, the center of their offense today as well.</i>

04:13.850 --> 04:15.610
<i>He's really in a period of rapid growth!</i>

04:15.610 --> 04:20.860
<i>As Toho piles up their victories, Sawada keeps on improving his skills.</i>

04:20.860 --> 04:21.440
Take it!

04:21.440 --> 04:22.780
Yeah!

04:22.780 --> 04:27.290
<i>Center forward Sorimachi takes on Hyuga's role as he's sitting on the bench.</i>

04:27.290 --> 04:29.370
<i>He's completely in sync with Sawada.</i>

04:31.640 --> 04:33.520
<i>It's perfect!</i>

04:33.520 --> 04:35.500
<i>Sorimachi scores a third goal in the waning minutes, like a killing blow!</i>

04:35.500 --> 04:37.250
FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL
HOKKAIDO

04:35.500 --> 04:39.750
<i>Even if Hyuga's not there, Toho's offensive power absolutely does not decrease!</i>

04:39.750 --> 04:41.270
<i>What's wrong, Hyuga?</i>

04:41.270 --> 04:44.180
<i>You're sitting on the bench... why don't you go out and play?</i>

04:45.280 --> 04:47.260
<i>But Chubu doesn't give up!</i>

04:47.260 --> 04:49.260
<i>They keep doggedly attacking Toho's goal.</i>

04:49.260 --> 04:51.980
<i>However, Toho has this man.</i>

04:51.980 --> 04:54.920
<i>The man with a clean sheet on him, Ken Wakashimazu!</i>

04:54.920 --> 04:57.370
<i>No one has scored against him yet this tournament.</i>

04:57.370 --> 04:59.190
<i>He's also the substitute captain.</i>

04:59.190 --> 05:00.780
<i>Bring it on...!</i>

05:01.590 --> 05:03.900
<i>He gets the ball up high in front of the goal.</i>

05:05.620 --> 05:06.320
What?

05:06.320 --> 05:08.990
<i>Wakashimazu easily catches it.</i>

05:08.990 --> 05:09.780
It's useless.

05:09.780 --> 05:11.780
We can't beat him in the air too.

05:13.030 --> 05:14.790
<i>The game ends!</i>

05:14.790 --> 05:16.550
<i>We did it! We won!</i>

05:16.550 --> 05:17.750
<i>We're in the best four!</i>

05:17.750 --> 05:19.450
<i>3-0!</i>

05:19.450 --> 05:21.380
<i>Toho Academy has won!</i>

05:21.380 --> 05:25.090
<i>And Wakashimazu keeps a clean sheet through his fourth game!</i>

05:25.090 --> 05:27.840
We did it!

05:27.840 --> 05:30.680
<i>Just one more game to go until the finals.</i>

05:31.240 --> 05:35.560
<i>Every player in Toho does their best to make up for Hyuga's absence.</i>

05:35.560 --> 05:38.750
<i>They keep honing their skills.</i>

05:38.750 --> 05:43.370
<i>What kind of team will they be if they add the powered-up Hyuga there?</i>

05:44.870 --> 05:47.820
<i>They are sure to be a fearsome and strong team.</i>

05:50.410 --> 05:53.300
All right! We're up next!

05:53.300 --> 05:54.540
Yeah!

05:56.520 --> 05:58.580
Matsuyama, wait a second.

05:59.380 --> 06:00.320
What is it?

06:02.100 --> 06:03.090
Yoshiko...

06:05.340 --> 06:07.840
What's the matter? Do you need me?

06:09.210 --> 06:10.920
Come on, Yoshiko!

06:10.920 --> 06:11.850
Yeah.

06:12.780 --> 06:14.700
Captain!

06:14.700 --> 06:16.100
What are you doing?

06:16.100 --> 06:17.220
Hurry up!

06:17.220 --> 06:19.100
Okay, I'm coming!

06:19.700 --> 06:21.360
Hey, what is it?

06:24.260 --> 06:27.110
D-do your best and win today too!

06:27.110 --> 06:29.360
O-okay...

06:29.360 --> 06:30.620
Was that all?

06:31.970 --> 06:32.910
Yes.

06:33.830 --> 06:35.450
Of course I will win.

06:37.080 --> 06:39.080
<i>What was that even about?</i>

06:39.080 --> 06:40.730
All right! Here we go, guys!

06:40.730 --> 06:42.050
Yeah!

06:43.490 --> 06:45.090
Oh, you...

06:45.530 --> 06:47.940
<i>I'm okay with this.</i>

06:49.060 --> 06:55.850
<i>After all, Matsuyama is only thinking about how to win this match right now.</i>

06:58.350 --> 06:59.560
Let's go, Furano!

06:59.560 --> 07:01.280
Fight, Furano!

07:01.280 --> 07:02.980
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

07:02.980 --> 07:05.980
<i>They're shouting as loudly as always.</i>

07:05.980 --> 07:07.980
<i>Furano Eleven, representing Hokkaido!</i>

07:07.980 --> 07:11.610
Good luck, good luck, Furano!

07:11.610 --> 07:16.490
<i>Their opponent, Minamiuwa MS from Ehime, are silently waiting for them.</i>

07:16.490 --> 07:18.230
<i>All good.</i>

07:18.230 --> 07:20.010
<i>We'll defeat Furano and be among the best four.</i>

07:20.010 --> 07:23.580
<i>Then we'll play against the previous champion, Nankatsu.</i>

07:23.580 --> 07:27.360
<i>This is the third quarter-final match with the semi-finals at stake:</i>

07:27.360 --> 07:29.470
<i>Furano MS vs. Minamiuwa MS.</i>

07:29.470 --> 07:31.010
<i>The game starts!</i>

07:32.130 --> 07:34.470
<i>Furano gets the ball first.</i>

07:34.470 --> 07:37.120
All right. We'll score the first goal today, too.

07:37.120 --> 07:37.770
Yeah!

07:37.770 --> 07:39.390
Bring it on, Matsuyama!

07:39.390 --> 07:43.130
<i>Minamiuwa's captain Ishida goes to check him!</i>

07:43.130 --> 07:45.650
<i>Is it a one-on-one fight between the captains right off the bat?</i>

07:45.650 --> 07:46.900
Here, Wakamatsu!

07:48.860 --> 07:50.950
Are you afraid of going up against me?

07:50.950 --> 07:53.500
I'm not afraid of you or anything.

07:53.500 --> 07:56.160
But football is a team sport. That's about it.

07:56.620 --> 07:58.620
Are you sure about that?

07:59.200 --> 08:02.120
It sounds better if you say you trust your friends,

08:02.120 --> 08:06.500
but doesn't that actually mean that you have no confidence in your ball controlling skills?

08:07.300 --> 08:10.170
<i>Minamiuwa performs a skillful pass cut this time.</i>

08:10.170 --> 08:11.670
Okay, come on!

08:11.670 --> 08:14.470
<i>Without a moment's delay, they send the ball to their captain, Ishida.</i>

08:15.220 --> 08:16.720
I'll do this in one go!

08:16.720 --> 08:17.930
Fall back, everyone!

08:17.930 --> 08:22.440
<i>Ishida is known for his technique, and he attacks with a solo dribble.</i>

08:22.440 --> 08:25.190
<i>Furano goes to mark him under Matsuyama's command.</i>

08:25.190 --> 08:27.980
<i>However, Minamiuwa immediately covers his sides.</i>

08:27.980 --> 08:29.360
Ishida!

08:31.250 --> 08:33.510
<i>Ishida breaks through the middle!</i>

08:33.510 --> 08:36.070
<i>Furano thought he'd pass the ball, letting him break through!</i>

08:36.070 --> 08:37.990
<i>Damn it! He is looking down on us!</i>

08:39.030 --> 08:39.740
Go!

08:39.740 --> 08:42.250
<i>However, Ishida cuts it short in front of the goal.</i>

08:43.010 --> 08:46.500
<i>Is this just a desperate tactic to evade Matsuyama's tackle?</i>

08:46.500 --> 08:47.970
<i>He just sent the ball up high?!</i>

08:47.970 --> 08:48.920
Okay!

08:50.760 --> 08:51.730
Here I go!

08:51.730 --> 08:54.150
<i>A player is running in from the sidelines!</i>

08:54.150 --> 08:56.760
<i>It's Minamiuwa's center forward, Takei!</i>

08:56.760 --> 08:58.510
Good! Go for it, Takei!

08:58.510 --> 08:59.140
What?!

08:59.980 --> 09:01.510
<i>Takei jumps!</i>

09:01.510 --> 09:04.100
<i>This is an aerial duel between him and the goalkeeper.</i>

09:07.240 --> 09:08.590
<i>Goal!</i>

09:08.590 --> 09:10.340
<i>Minamiuwa opens the score.</i>

09:10.340 --> 09:11.860
<i>Takei wins this duel!</i>

09:12.780 --> 09:14.450
They got ahead of Furano first?

09:14.450 --> 09:16.200
You did it, Takei!

09:16.200 --> 09:17.050
You bet I did.

09:17.050 --> 09:19.660
Them being a championship contender means nothing to me!

09:19.660 --> 09:22.310
<i>This is an unexpected development!</i>

09:22.310 --> 09:26.710
<i>It's the first time in this tournament that Furano gave up the first goal.</i>

09:26.710 --> 09:28.460
Matsuyama...

09:28.460 --> 09:31.880
<i>Despite being seen as the underdogs, Minamiuwa takes the initiative!</i>

09:31.880 --> 09:36.380
<i>How will Furano get back on their feet after this?</i>

09:36.380 --> 09:39.010
<i>Please win, Matsuyama. Please...</i>

09:41.470 --> 09:44.340
<i>Furano gathers their spirits back and attacks.</i>

09:45.600 --> 09:46.730
<i>What?!</i>

09:49.560 --> 09:50.300
All right!

09:50.300 --> 09:52.190
<i>Minamiuwa cuts the pass again.</i>

09:52.190 --> 09:54.040
Once more! Let's score another one!

09:54.040 --> 09:56.150
<i>Did that first goal boost their morale?</i>

09:56.150 --> 09:58.150
<i>Minamiuwa's got some nice moves.</i>

09:58.150 --> 10:00.660
Guys! Don't panic just because we lost the first goal.

10:00.660 --> 10:03.240
Just calm down and show them the results of our training!

10:03.240 --> 10:04.370
Yeah!

10:04.950 --> 10:06.330
Okay!

10:06.330 --> 10:09.220
<i>I wonder if Furano's mood has changed after Matsuyama's words.</i>

10:09.220 --> 10:11.060
<i>This time, they cut the pass.</i>

10:11.060 --> 10:12.250
For you, captain!

10:12.250 --> 10:13.550
All right!

10:13.550 --> 10:16.640
<i>They are completely reading through our passing at the moment.</i>

10:16.640 --> 10:17.340
<i>If that's so...</i>

10:19.550 --> 10:20.400
<i>Then I'll do it myself!</i>

10:20.400 --> 10:22.400
<i>Matsuyama dashes for the opposing goal!</i>

10:22.400 --> 10:24.810
<i>He's showing off his smooth ball-keeping skills!</i>

10:24.810 --> 10:27.140
Crap! He didn't go for a pass!

10:27.140 --> 10:29.650
<i>Will Matsuyama keep it and and shoot?</i>

10:30.230 --> 10:31.600
That's Matsuyama for you.

10:31.600 --> 10:33.670
Too bad, I knew you'd try to do this!

10:33.670 --> 10:35.400
I won't let you shoot!

10:36.610 --> 10:40.610
<i>Just when we thought he was going to shoot, Matsuyama ends up sending a pass!</i>

10:40.610 --> 10:41.450
What?!

10:41.450 --> 10:43.120
Oda! Assist for you!

10:43.540 --> 10:45.660
<i>Ball gets to the unmarked Oda!</i>

10:45.660 --> 10:47.380
Okay! I've got this!

10:47.380 --> 10:49.580
<i>Oda takes aim and shoots!</i>

10:50.250 --> 10:52.530
<i>He misses!</i>

10:53.210 --> 10:54.550
What?!

10:54.550 --> 10:56.420
I got lucky.

10:57.360 --> 10:58.650
Don't mind! Don't mind!

10:58.650 --> 11:01.480
Don't sweat it. Stuff like that happens.

11:01.480 --> 11:02.930
I'm sorry.

11:03.860 --> 11:05.930
<i>Looks like lady luck is on our side.</i>

11:09.190 --> 11:10.980
All right, let's go for another goal!

11:11.420 --> 11:13.030
<i>It's a chance for Minamiuwa.</i>

11:13.030 --> 11:15.770
<i>Ishida sends the ball towards the goal.</i>

11:15.770 --> 11:17.650
Do you really think we'd fall for the same trick?

11:17.650 --> 11:18.820
Do not underestimate...

11:18.820 --> 11:19.990
...Furano MS!

11:22.030 --> 11:24.660
<i>This time, all the defenders stop the attack.</i>

11:26.660 --> 11:28.150
Nice defense!

11:28.150 --> 11:30.330
<i>Furano protects their goal this time.</i>

11:30.330 --> 11:33.330
Whew. That was pretty dangerous.

11:33.330 --> 11:35.480
Furano is having an unexpectedly hard time.

11:35.480 --> 11:37.240
Minamiuwa, huh...

11:37.240 --> 11:39.720
This must be what they call a "dark horse"...

11:40.100 --> 11:41.240
<i>That's right.</i>

11:41.240 --> 11:43.450
<i>We need to be careful too.</i>

11:47.220 --> 11:48.350
Damn it!

11:48.940 --> 11:51.440
<i>The first half ends here.</i>

11:51.440 --> 11:53.350
<i>What are you dawdling around for?</i>

11:53.350 --> 11:54.870
<i>1-0!</i>

11:54.870 --> 11:57.360
<i>It ends with Minamiuwa leading the score by one goal.</i>

11:57.360 --> 12:00.610
Let's go. We should start warming up too.

12:00.610 --> 12:01.520
Yeah.

12:01.520 --> 12:04.370
We don't want to struggle against a dark horse.

12:04.370 --> 12:07.400
Oh no! At this rate, we'll lose...

12:07.400 --> 12:08.020
Yeah.

12:08.020 --> 12:09.500
What do you mean, "yeah"?!

12:09.500 --> 12:15.300
Yoshiko, if we lose, you'll be leaving Matsuyama today forever!

12:16.540 --> 12:18.530
<i>Got it, Yoshiko?</i>

12:18.530 --> 12:21.970
<i>Your dad is waiting for us in the US.</i>

12:21.970 --> 12:26.770
<i>I'm sorry. We were going to join him right after the first term ended, but—</i>

12:26.770 --> 12:33.730
<i>You've worked hard as a manager so far, so I understand you wanting the see them until the final match, but...</i>

12:33.730 --> 12:37.060
<i>I will leave right away if we lose.</i>

12:37.060 --> 12:38.800
<i>I guess that'll be all right.</i>

12:38.800 --> 12:39.730
<i>Yes.</i>

12:41.000 --> 12:43.070
Matsuyama...

12:53.120 --> 12:55.580
MINAMIUWA MIDDLE SCHOOL
EHIME PREFECTURE

12:54.370 --> 12:55.580
All right.

12:55.580 --> 12:58.090
Excellent work in the first half guys.

12:58.090 --> 13:00.350
The weather will get much hotter.

13:00.350 --> 13:02.290
Our opponent is going to get exhausted.

13:02.290 --> 13:04.200
Stick to the plan. Show no weakness!

13:04.200 --> 13:05.090
Yes, sir!

13:05.090 --> 13:08.140
We'll get another one in second half and win.

13:08.140 --> 13:09.100
Yeah.

13:09.100 --> 13:10.850
FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL
HOKKAIDO PREFECTURE

13:10.850 --> 13:13.310
Sorry, this one's on me.

13:13.310 --> 13:14.650
If I'd scored that one...

13:14.650 --> 13:16.970
Don't sweat over it, Oda.

13:16.970 --> 13:17.900
Yeah.

13:17.900 --> 13:19.440
Just work hard in the second half.

13:19.440 --> 13:20.610
Sure.

13:20.610 --> 13:22.130
There's still 30 minutes left.

13:22.130 --> 13:23.320
Let's calm down and continue.

13:23.320 --> 13:25.360
We can't do anything about the goal we conceded.

13:25.360 --> 13:27.320
First, we have to tie the game.

13:27.320 --> 13:29.800
If we do that, we can establish our rhythm and win.

13:29.800 --> 13:31.670
Have confidence, guys!

13:31.670 --> 13:32.580
Yes, sir!

13:33.260 --> 13:34.380
<i>Damn!</i>

13:34.380 --> 13:38.670
<i>If we're already struggling at this point, there is no way we'll become champions.</i>

13:38.670 --> 13:39.620
Don't lose!

13:39.620 --> 13:43.670
<i>The sun shines even brighter now and it's about 36°C degrees now.</i>

13:43.670 --> 13:47.220
<i>It will be a battle against the heat, as well.</i>

13:47.220 --> 13:49.720
<i>The second half is finally starting.</i>

13:49.720 --> 13:52.380
<i>I believe in you, Matsuyama.</i>

13:52.380 --> 13:53.640
<i>I believe in you.</i>

13:55.680 --> 13:57.930
<i>Minamiuwa is attacking aggressively!</i>

13:57.930 --> 13:59.460
<i>They are aiming for a second goal.</i>

13:59.460 --> 14:00.700
Here we go!

14:00.700 --> 14:03.150
We will score another and finish this match off.

14:03.150 --> 14:04.280
Don't lose your wits!

14:04.280 --> 14:06.360
We won't allow a second one no matter what!

14:09.820 --> 14:12.510
<i>Minamiuwa is a fine team indeed.</i>

14:12.510 --> 14:16.330
<i>It's no coincidence that they were able to keep this game at 1-0 so far.</i>

14:16.330 --> 14:18.040
<i>But of course.</i>

14:18.040 --> 14:22.330
<i>Minamiuwa is the strongest team I've coached in my career.</i>

14:22.330 --> 14:28.340
<i>They came at the top in Shikoku, and now this team will dominate in the National Tournament.</i>

14:29.140 --> 14:31.350
<i>A precise attack from Minamiuwa!</i>

14:31.350 --> 14:34.220
<i>On the other hand, has Hokkaido's Furano,</i>

14:34.220 --> 14:36.890
<i>who aren't used to this heat, started to lose their stamina?</i>

14:36.890 --> 14:38.130
<i>Do your best!</i>

14:38.130 --> 14:39.900
<i>Grit your teeth, guys!</i>

14:42.150 --> 14:44.120
<i>What's wrong, Matsuyama?</i>

14:44.120 --> 14:46.440
<i>Weren't you going to pay me back?!</i>

14:46.440 --> 14:47.640
<i>Damn it!</i>

14:47.640 --> 14:49.700
<i>If we concede the second goal, it's all over.</i>

14:49.700 --> 14:52.410
<i>We are the ones who know this most!</i>

14:53.420 --> 14:54.410
<i>He got the ball!</i>

14:54.410 --> 14:57.020
<i>The keystone of the team, Furano's captain Matsuyama!</i>

14:57.020 --> 14:58.710
<i>He finally manages to steal the ball!</i>

15:00.210 --> 15:02.470
<i>He brings up the ball by himself!</i>

15:02.470 --> 15:05.920
<i>He is dubbed as the player with the best ball control in this tournament.</i>

15:05.920 --> 15:07.380
Kaneda!

15:07.380 --> 15:09.760
<i>His pass accuracy is also second to none!</i>

15:09.760 --> 15:12.760
<i>Truly, he's the commander of Furano, Hikaru Matsuyama!</i>

15:12.760 --> 15:13.970
Matsuyama!

15:14.380 --> 15:15.390
Nice pass!

15:15.390 --> 15:16.420
Read their passes!

15:16.420 --> 15:17.470
We need to stop them!

15:19.180 --> 15:20.230
Take it!

15:20.230 --> 15:24.360
<i>A rare long pass from Furano, which usually relies on short passes.</i>

15:25.320 --> 15:26.470
It's bad, turn back!

15:26.470 --> 15:27.990
Tighten the front of the goal!

15:27.990 --> 15:30.030
I'll send a cross before you can!

15:30.030 --> 15:31.780
<i>It's a superb cross!</i>

15:31.780 --> 15:33.160
<i>The ball is sent to Oda!</i>

15:33.160 --> 15:34.280
This time...!

15:36.240 --> 15:39.500
<i>It's right to the keeper!</i>

15:39.500 --> 15:41.320
<i>That's a tough one.</i>

15:41.320 --> 15:43.700
<i>Oda missed another chance to score.</i>

15:43.700 --> 15:45.170
<i>Now it makes two.</i>

15:45.170 --> 15:46.520
Oda...

15:46.520 --> 15:49.010
All right, send it before it's late!

15:49.010 --> 15:50.920
Matsuyama won't be able to return!

15:51.500 --> 15:54.180
<i>A counter-attack from Minamiuwa!</i>

15:54.180 --> 15:55.550
Guys, I'm counting on you!

15:55.550 --> 15:56.980
<i>God, I beg you.</i>

15:56.980 --> 15:58.770
<i>Let them win.</i>

15:58.770 --> 16:03.480
<i>It's too cruel to Yoshiko and Matsuyama to be apart like this.</i>

16:06.760 --> 16:08.940
<i>Takei is marked.</i>

16:08.940 --> 16:10.240
Then...

16:10.240 --> 16:11.450
Time to shoot!

16:11.930 --> 16:14.530
<i>Ishida went for a long shot suddenly.</i>

16:16.920 --> 16:18.470
<i>He catches it!</i>

16:18.470 --> 16:20.120
<i>The goalkeeper makes a great play!</i>

16:20.120 --> 16:22.120
<i>It's an outstanding save from Kato.</i>

16:22.870 --> 16:24.080
Come on, Kato!

16:24.080 --> 16:26.510
It's about time we stop showing them such a slugfest!

16:26.510 --> 16:29.380
Do you really think Furano can lose to such a team?!

16:29.970 --> 16:31.010
Captain...!

16:31.010 --> 16:32.380
Matsuyama!

16:32.380 --> 16:33.380
Captain!

16:33.380 --> 16:36.430
<i>Kato, who protected his goal with an excellent play,</i>

16:36.430 --> 16:38.430
<i>sends a long pass to his captain, Matsuyama.</i>

16:39.770 --> 16:40.600
All right!

16:41.390 --> 16:43.690
<i>Can Furano catch up with them and take the lead?!</i>

16:43.690 --> 16:46.150
<i>Only ten minutes remain in the match.</i>

16:46.150 --> 16:48.140
Follow the captain's lead, guys!

16:48.140 --> 16:49.410
It's just as captain says!

16:49.410 --> 16:52.530
Are we going to lose against these guys?!

16:52.530 --> 16:53.510
He is right!

16:53.510 --> 16:56.530
We can't afford to lose here!

16:56.530 --> 16:58.530
Follow the captain's lead!

16:59.810 --> 17:01.060
<i>Th-this is...</i>

17:01.060 --> 17:03.040
<i>Furano attacks with all of their players!</i>

17:03.040 --> 17:05.290
<i>They all run, aiming for the goal!</i>

17:05.290 --> 17:07.540
They've sure got a lot of spirit left.

17:07.540 --> 17:10.330
<i>You can really see Furano values teamwork above all else...</i>

17:10.330 --> 17:13.090
<i>Everyone's united with a single command from Matsuyama.</i>

17:13.090 --> 17:14.590
Matsuyama...

17:14.590 --> 17:16.010
Don't panic, guys!

17:16.010 --> 17:17.240
We still have 10 minutes!

17:17.240 --> 17:21.600
If we keep reading their passes, Furano can't score a goal against us!

17:21.600 --> 17:23.060
Yeah...

17:25.270 --> 17:26.940
Matsuyama...

17:26.940 --> 17:27.940
<i>Damn it...</i>

17:27.940 --> 17:30.770
<i>I won't lose to guys like these!</i>

17:31.220 --> 17:32.900
<i>Hey, football club!</i>

17:33.900 --> 17:37.280
<i>Your time's up. It's our turn to use the gymnasium.</i>

17:37.280 --> 17:38.660
<i>Okay!</i>

17:38.660 --> 17:42.080
<i>All right! We'll just clean the front the goal and keep practising.</i>

17:42.080 --> 17:42.950
<i>Yes!</i>

17:42.950 --> 17:43.660
<i>Here!</i>

17:45.830 --> 17:47.440
<i>Damn it...</i>

17:47.440 --> 17:50.130
<i>We can't practice like this.</i>

17:55.040 --> 17:56.840
<i>Damn it all!</i>

17:56.840 --> 18:01.260
<i>There's no way we'll lose to guys who play</i>

18:04.640 --> 18:06.560
<i>on the ground, on bare earth year-round!</i>

18:14.960 --> 18:18.990
<i>Matsuyama doesn't even pass before firing off a long, long shot!</i>

18:18.990 --> 18:20.240
What?!

18:20.240 --> 18:22.030
It's our captain's special shot!

18:22.030 --> 18:24.700
<i>It's a sharp shot that looks like it's crawling on the ground!</i>

18:24.700 --> 18:29.290
<i>Minamiuwa, who's been reading their passing so far, is completely fooled!</i>

18:32.000 --> 18:33.430
<i>Goal!</i>

18:33.430 --> 18:36.340
<i>A long shot with all of Matsuyama's strength behind it!</i>

18:36.340 --> 18:39.240
<i>Furano finally ties the game!</i>

18:39.240 --> 18:43.850
<i>Unlike you, we had to keep on practicing, even in those circumstances.</i>

18:43.850 --> 18:47.100
We'll show you our determination—
we who have worked through the snow!

18:47.780 --> 18:51.850
<i>That's the kind of shot he can fire with power built through training on difficult ground.</i>

18:51.850 --> 18:53.900
<i>That's what you call a Northern Country Shot!</i>

18:53.900 --> 18:55.470
You did it, captain!

18:55.470 --> 18:56.400
We caught up!

18:56.400 --> 18:58.400
We did it, Yoshiko! We have caught up!

18:58.400 --> 18:59.400
Yeah!

18:59.400 --> 19:02.170
That was an awesome shot.

19:02.170 --> 19:05.580
<i>Matsuyama's been hiding that kind of fighting spirit...</i>

19:06.160 --> 19:09.580
<i>Still, that long shot that crawls on the ground...</i>

19:09.580 --> 19:11.480
<i>It's terribly powerful.</i>

19:11.500 --> 19:16.340
He can fire a shot like that because he's been strengthening his lower body in a snowy land, right?

19:16.340 --> 19:20.350
Yeah. And the others successfully positioned themselves to receive a pass,

19:20.350 --> 19:22.930
forcing the defense to be unable to focus solely on Matsuyama.

19:22.930 --> 19:25.930
It's as if they scored that tying goal with all eleven players.

19:27.100 --> 19:30.100
<i>You still need another goal, Matsuyama.</i>

19:30.100 --> 19:33.310
<i>Furano's riding the tide after tying the game.</i>

19:33.770 --> 19:35.980
<i>They cut the pass!</i>

19:35.980 --> 19:36.980
Watch out!

19:36.980 --> 19:38.740
Matsuyama can do more than pass!

19:38.740 --> 19:41.030
He can also dribble and fire long shots!

19:42.110 --> 19:43.810
The others can only pass the ball!

19:43.810 --> 19:45.120
Read their pass course!

19:45.560 --> 19:47.420
<i>Kaneda breaks through with his dribbles.</i>

19:47.420 --> 19:48.120
What?

19:48.120 --> 19:52.080
<i>This is a complete attack that incorporates the basics of football, dribbling and passing.</i>

19:52.080 --> 19:53.330
Guys...

19:53.330 --> 19:57.710
Furano's guys looked exhausted, but it seems they are doing just fine.

19:57.710 --> 20:00.220
No. They're all battling through fatigue now.

20:00.220 --> 20:03.840
And Matsuyama's the one who's holding everyone together.

20:03.840 --> 20:05.890
Guys, keep fighting!

20:06.850 --> 20:11.020
<i>The ball gets to Matsuyama once again, right in front of Minamiuwa's goal!</i>

20:11.020 --> 20:12.980
I won't let you score again!

20:12.980 --> 20:17.110
Ishida, I'll take you on personally just like you wished!

20:17.930 --> 20:19.300
<i>Matsuyama's at it!</i>

20:19.300 --> 20:22.450
<i>He's planning to get past Ishida the Technician all by himself!</i>

20:22.450 --> 20:23.910
Matsuyama!

20:23.910 --> 20:25.660
You think you can get past me?

20:25.660 --> 20:26.660
I sure do!

20:28.220 --> 20:29.800
<i>He got past him!</i>

20:29.800 --> 20:33.330
<i>Matsuyama clearly wins this fight between captains!</i>

20:34.140 --> 20:37.840
Ishida was passed... He lost in terms of ball technique...

20:37.840 --> 20:40.300
<i>There's no one to mark Matsuyama in front of the goal!</i>

20:40.300 --> 20:41.780
<i>It's a huge chance!</i>

20:41.780 --> 20:42.380
Take this!

20:42.380 --> 20:43.090
What?

20:44.240 --> 20:44.970
Captain!

20:44.970 --> 20:47.200
This one's yours, Oda!

20:47.200 --> 20:49.810
You are Furano's center forward!

20:49.810 --> 20:51.410
He's right. Just shoot, Oda!

20:51.410 --> 20:53.310
Do it like you always do during practice!

20:53.310 --> 20:54.760
<i>Captain...</i>

20:54.760 --> 20:56.190
<i>Everyone...</i>

20:56.190 --> 20:58.540
<i>Even though I failed you twice today, you...</i>

20:59.470 --> 21:00.670
<i>Damn it!</i>

21:00.670 --> 21:03.030
<i>I can't call myself a man if I don't score here!</i>

21:03.030 --> 21:04.650
Go!

21:07.620 --> 21:08.660
<i>It's in!</i>

21:08.660 --> 21:14.500
<i>The third time's the charm, and this time, he makes sure to splendidly convert this chance!</i>

21:14.500 --> 21:16.530
I... I did it!

21:16.530 --> 21:17.750
<i>Furano turns the tables!</i>

21:18.350 --> 21:20.400
<i>They're in the lead, 2-1!</i>

21:20.400 --> 21:22.260
<i>All is good.</i>

21:22.260 --> 21:23.570
Damn it...

21:23.570 --> 21:25.180
They got ahead of us!

21:27.060 --> 21:30.440
<i>The final whistle is blown and the match is over!</i>

21:30.440 --> 21:36.100
<i>Minamiuwa MS finally runs out of strength and Furano finds a place for themselves among the best four with this comeback win!</i>

21:36.100 --> 21:37.480
We won!

21:37.480 --> 21:39.840
All right! Nankatsu's next!

21:39.840 --> 21:41.730
And we'll get Toho in the final!

21:41.730 --> 21:44.240
<i>So you won, Matsuyama...</i>

21:44.240 --> 21:46.990
Just what you'd expect from the persistent Furano.

21:46.990 --> 21:48.940
<i>That last goal...</i>

21:48.940 --> 21:52.000
<i>Matsuyama could have easily scored that himself.</i>

21:52.000 --> 21:56.340
<i>But, he deliberately sent a pass to Oda, who was in bad form today.</i>

21:56.340 --> 21:57.800
<i>Matsuyama...</i>

21:57.800 --> 22:01.630
<i>Your belief in your teammates runs that deep, huh...?</i>

22:01.630 --> 22:04.250
We won! We won, Yoshiko!

22:04.250 --> 22:06.380
Yeah... I'm so glad!

22:06.380 --> 22:08.130
Manager!

22:08.130 --> 22:10.130
We won today too!

22:10.130 --> 22:11.700
Matsuyama...

22:13.950 --> 22:15.260
<i>Fujisawa...</i>

22:15.260 --> 22:18.570
<i>Your final memory with us will be what you wish for. </i>

22:38.870 --> 22:44.920
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.870 --> 22:44.920
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.920 --> 22:50.930
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.920 --> 22:50.930
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.930 --> 22:56.980
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.930 --> 22:56.980
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.980 --> 23:01.610
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.980 --> 23:01.610
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:07.900
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:07.900
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.330
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.330
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.330 --> 23:21.370
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.370 --> 23:25.840
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.370 --> 23:25.840
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.130 --> 23:33.470
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.130 --> 23:33.470
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.470 --> 23:39.520
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.520 --> 23:45.820
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.520 --> 23:45.820
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.150 --> 24:00.720
COMING UP; EPISODE 41:
THE FEARSOME DARK HORSE
